{
  "_comment": [
    "Composite indexes required by server-side and client-issued queries.",
    "Firestore can serve a single equality filter with an orderBy on the SAME field, and can merge",
    "several equality-only filters from its automatic single-field indexes. Anything else — an",
    "equality filter plus an orderBy on a DIFFERENT field, an array-contains alongside an equality",
    "filter, or a range plus an orderBy — needs an explicit composite index, and without one",
    "Firestore FAILS the query rather than answering it slowly.",
    "",
    "Deploy with:",
    "  firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes",
    "Building them takes a few minutes on a large collection, so do it before an exam window, not",
    "during one. `firebase firestore:indexes` prints the current state.",
    "",
    "attempts: mirrors exactly what AttemptController passes — a school caller is always scoped to",
    "schoolId and a student caller to studentId, with examId and status as optional filters, ordered",
    "by startTime, score or endTime descending. FirestoreAttemptDao falls back to a capped in-memory",
    "page when a query fails, so a missing index here degrades performance instead of breaking a",
    "dashboard.",
    "",
    "exams: FirestoreExamDao.findPublishedForSchool runs BOTH exam queries below on every student",
    "dashboard load (the locked 'Soon' preview in getUpcomingListItems), and SchoolStudentOnboarding",
    "runs the status+createdAt one when staff pick an exam to trigger. Unlike attempts, ExamDao has",
    "NO in-memory fallback — a missing index here is a 500 on the student's Upcoming tab, not slow.",
    "",
    "users / proctoring_logs: the school candidate roster (schoolId+role, ordered and optionally",
    "name-range-searched) and the live proctoring wall (schoolId + timestamp desc)."
  ],
